From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 130] panvk: cache decoded BC7 texels, refine single-subset modes directly
Generated-by: LLM

The BC7 encoder decoded every texel (index bit extraction, anchors,
partition and weight tables, rotation) on each of its passes, about
160 decodes per block, and its 16-texel loops spilled.

Decode the 16 texels once per block into workgroup shared memory (a
private array spilled 9000 times), keep the encoder's per-texel loops
rolled, and run the dual-plane candidate first so the single-plane
encode can stop after its covariance pass when the energy off the best
RGBA line already exceeds the dual-plane error.

Mode 6 blocks (one RGBA line, the bulk of real BC7) start the refits on
their own endpoints instead of a principal-axis fit and skip the
dual-plane candidate. Opaque unrotated mode 5 blocks transfer exactly:
their 2-bit colour indices are the ASTC 2-bit weights and the 8-bit
endpoints fit. All candidates keep compile-time layouts; a single
runtime-parameterised call site measured slower (81 spills).
biblioklept

PSNR equal or higher on random, smooth and real BC7 (Assassin's Creed
Rogue textures encoded with bc7enc, modes 1/5/6/7): +0.01 to +0.28 dB
on real data.

Mali-G615 MC2, one 2048x2048 level, shader time: random 174 -> 56 ms,
smooth 145 -> 36 ms, real opaque 143-156 -> 33-35 ms, real alpha
119-128 -> 37-45 ms.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/129

